#### **2. Design & Technical Specification**

**2.1. High-Level Architecture**
The refactor will use the native HTML **`<template>`** element. This approach is superior to `innerHTML` because the content is parsed by the browser once at page load (but not rendered), making it inert and safe. Cloning this content via JavaScript is highly performant and maintains a clean separation of concerns: HTML structure lives in the `.html` file, and JS logic lives in the `.js` file.

**2.2. Component Interaction Flow**
1.  **Init:** `AppInitializer` creates and initializes `sidePanelManager`.
2.  **Content Injection:** `sidePanelManager.init()` reads from the `<template>` elements, populates image sources from the `infoPanelContent.js` asset manifest, and injects the final content into the DOM.
3.  **Event Binding:** `EventBinder` attaches a single delegated click listener to the tab container.
4.  **User Interaction:** User clicks a tab.
5.  **Delegation:** `EventBinder` calls `sidePanelManager.handleTabClick()`.
6.  **State Change:** `sidePanelManager` updates the `.active` classes on tabs and content panes, and plays a sound via `audioManager`.

**2.3. DOM Structure Changes (`index.html`)**
The content within `#control-deck` will be refactored as follows:

```html
<!-- In index.html -->
<div id="control-deck" class="side-panel left-panel">
    <div class="expanded-view">
        <!-- ... panel header ... -->
        <div class="panel-content">
            <!-- These containers will now be empty -->
            <div id="about-tab" class="panel-tab-content active"></div>
            <div id="highlights-tab" class="panel-tab-content"></div>
            <div id="settings-tab" class="panel-tab-content"></div>
        </div>
    </div>
    
    <!-- The content is moved into inert <template> tags -->
    <template id="about-tab-template">
        <p>HUE 9000 explores diagetic design...</p>
    </template>
    
    <template id="highlights-tab-template">
        <h3>The Living Lens</h3>
        <p>The central lens uses dynamic gradients...</p>
        <!-- Note the use of data-src-key and the absent src -->
        <img data-src-key="HAL9000-lens.png" alt="..." class="panel-image">
        <!-- ... more content ... -->
    </template>
    
    <template id="settings-tab-template">
        <h3>System Settings</h3>
        <div class="settings-group">
            <!-- ... haptics toggle ... -->
        </div>
    </template>
</div>
```

**2.4. Module-by-Module Implementation Plan**
*   **`sidePanelManager.js`**
    *   **`init()`:** Will be updated to call a sequence of new private methods: `_injectContentFromTemplates()`, `_populateImageSources()`, `_initImageObserver()`, and `_syncInitialControlState()`.
    *   **`_injectContentFromTemplates()`:** Will query for all `<template>` elements inside `#control-deck`, clone their `content`, and append it to the corresponding empty `.panel-tab-content` div.
    *   **`_populateImageSources()`:** After content is injected, this will query for all `<img>` tags with a `data-src-key` attribute and set their `src` from the imported `panelImagePaths` manifest.
    *   **`_syncInitialControlState()`:** Will query for the haptics toggle and set its initial `checked` state based on `appState.getIsHapticsEnabled()`.
    *   **`handleTabClick(event)`:** Will contain the logic to switch tabs, ensuring it checks if the clicked tab is already active to prevent re-playing the audio.
*   **`EventBinder.js`**
    *   The complex tab-switching logic will be removed.
    *   In `_bindSidePanelControls`, it will add a single delegated event listener to the `.panel-tabs` container, which will call `sidePanelManager.handleTabClick(event)`.
    *   The haptics toggle listener will be added here, and it will correctly `dispatch(actions.setHapticsEnabled(checkedState))`.
*   **`infoPanelContent.js`**
    *   This file will be simplified. It will no longer contain HTML strings. It will only import the four panel images and export them in a single `panelImagePaths` object, mapping a key (the filename) to the Vite-processed path.
*   **`actions.js`**
    *   A new action type `SET_HAPTICS_ENABLED` and a corresponding action creator `setHapticsEnabled(isEnabled)` will be added.
*   **`actionHandler.js`**
    *   A new `case` will be added to `handleAction` for `SET_HAPTICS_ENABLED`. It will call `appState.setIsHapticsEnabled(action.payload.isEnabled)`.
*   **`_variables-structural.css`**
    *   A new token, `--space-5xl: 6rem;`, will be added to the spacing scale.
*   **`_side-panels.css`**
    *   The `margin` on `.panel-content img.panel-image` will be changed from `6rem` to use the new `var(--space-5xl)` token.

